{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/892009-building-my-reckoning-s-hunter","id":892009,"title":"Building my Reckoning's Hunter...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-16T14:24:52-07:00","id":892009,"title":"Building my Reckoning's Hunter...","content":"I'm trying to build up my Reckoning's Hunter character. I feel some attraction for the defender creed, but I don't like to come up with a zealot which see everything black or white. I'm looking for a character able to discern between &quot;good&quot; monsters and &quot;evil&quot; mosters. Do you have any hint for me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T14:32:33-07:00","id":892015,"title":"","content":"Well, as a Defender you could focus more on protecting the innocent. Maybe you see that monsters can also be victims, or be worthy of protection, or you just don\u00b4t care to hunt monsters that seem like they're doing no harm (focusing on the dangerous ones). Defenders may be zealots, but that's not to say that they're a bunch of fanatics killing all that's &quot;unclean&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-16-2016, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T15:11:01-07:00","id":892049,"title":"","content":"Zeal isn't the same as thinking of monsters solely as evil. Zeal is about dedication to an ideal. Defenders and Judges are both noted as being prone to having the idea of &quot;acceptable&quot; monsters that don't violate those Hunter's ideals. If a particular character's ideal that they're zealous about is, &quot;protect humans from monsters,&quot; they're probably going to not treat all supernaturals are monsters, and only target ones that actively prey on humans, a well as go after humans that cross enough lines.<br /> <br /> If you have access to the Creedbooks, they detail &quot;camps&quot; for each Creed to demonstrate how different individuals interpret their Virtue, Creed, and place in the world. Temperate Defenders tend to cling to something from before their Imbuing and tend to assess supernaturals based on the level of threat they pose to that anchor; such as a cop that that sees keeping their precinct clean of corruption (supernatural and not) is the best way to keep people safe. Tolerant Defenders are generally Defenders that started as more intellectual and thoughtful in life, so they tend to value practicality and planning over rashly chasing every monster they come across; they're noted as being the Defenders most likely to pick up Innocence path Edges to help them ensure maximum information gathering where most other Zeal based characters look down on the idea of adopting the thinking of the Innocents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T15:31:34-07:00","id":892066,"title":"","content":"Indeed I was thinking about a character with some contacts or even allies among vampires or werewolves... but I was afraid that as a zealot, a defender may be pretty close minded to have business with monsters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T15:37:54-07:00","id":892069,"title":"","content":"I think you could easily stick with a Defender and play the character how you'd like; that is, protecting the innocent(whether that's a supernatural or a human). Just play as a Tolerant Defender.<br /> <br /> If that doesn't work out for you, then perhaps a Redeemer may be more to your liking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T15:50:38-07:00","id":892078,"title":"","content":"A Judge might be more appropriate as one of the hallmarks of that Creed is the discerning between &quot;good&quot; monsters and &quot;bad&quot; monsters. Y'know, <i>judging</i>.<br /> <br /> An Innocent might be more prone to &quot;friends&quot; among the supernatural community, but it's not like that's <i>only </i>them, just more common.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T11:48:04-07:00","id":892666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/892009-building-my-reckoning-s-hunter?p=892078#post892078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Judge might be more appropriate as one of the hallmarks of that Creed is the discerning between &quot;good&quot; monsters and &quot;bad&quot; monsters. Y'know, <i>judging</i>.<br /> <br /> An Innocent might be more prone to &quot;friends&quot; among the supernatural community, but it's not like that's <i>only </i>them, just more common.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Judges and redeamers would be more to the concept the OP has than an Avenger or Defender IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T23:37:28-07:00","id":893074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/892009-building-my-reckoning-s-hunter?p=892066#post892066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed I was thinking about a character with some contacts or even allies among vampires or werewolves... but I was afraid that as a zealot, a defender may be pretty close minded to have business with monsters</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are going for a Defender then what is he going to defend? Each Defender has the one thing that he wants to preserve above all else, so IF you indeed have supernatural contacts and allies they may be involved with the community you want to preserve in positive fashion. Let's say it's a community. Maybe the werewolves have kinfolk in there (then the kinfolk would probably be your contacts) or a vampire has claimed it as his domain for personal reasons but actually feeds somewhere else.<br /> <br /> Virtue wise you probably should mix your zeal with a bit of mercy considering your approach. Also you can invest one of your starting Zeal points into the Edge &quot;Discern&quot; which helps you discern between good and evil monsters. Alternativly you could start stacking Mercy in play to go either for Witness or Illuminate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T10:30:59-07:00","id":893422,"title":"","content":"One thing i can't understand is how imbued CAN have supernatural allies/contacts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T10:40:57-07:00","id":893430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/892009-building-my-reckoning-s-hunter?p=893422#post893422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing i can't understand is how imbued CAN have supernatural allies/contacts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same way a Kindred could have a Garou as a contact or a Changeling could have a scientist for a contact: carefully and gently as possible.<br /> <br /> Granted, there are numerous other Imbued who'd have a problem with it, but it's still not impossible. Just unlikely and difficult to maintain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T10:56:17-07:00","id":893439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/892009-building-my-reckoning-s-hunter?p=893430#post893430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same way a Kindred could have a Garou as a contact or a Changeling could have a scientist for a contact: carefully and gently as possible.<br /> <br /> Granted, there are numerous other Imbued who'd have a problem with it, but it's still not impossible. Just unlikely and difficult to maintain.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it's not as if it's not supported by the books: one of the Hermit book's narrators ends up with supernatural contacts, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:36:30-07:00","id":893486,"title":"","content":"Plus the Innocent and Redeemer Creeds are build around non-violent interaction with supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T15:58:21-07:00","id":893694,"title":"","content":"There are even traits in the books for representing such relationships.<br /> <br /> Creedbook <i>Avenger</i> includes the Pawn Background to have a supernatural character backing your Hunt (assumed to be for their own gain of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T21:55:24-07:00","id":894561,"title":"","content":"True, but for me it was always strange how a group of super powered individuals dedicated to hunting DOWN all other supers, would have those supers as allies/friends/contacts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T23:15:43-07:00","id":894574,"title":"","content":"The Imbued are not organized, or unified, enough to call them a group of individuals dedicated to hunting down all other supers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T23:53:47-07:00","id":894584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/892009-building-my-reckoning-s-hunter?p=894574#post894574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Imbued are not organized, or unified, enough to call them a group of individuals dedicated to hunting down all other supers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, why do Innocents and Redeemers exist if the imbued are only about hunting supernaturals down?<br /> <br /> <i>As a splat</i>, the imbued are called to engage with the supernatural, but that engagement can run from hunting them down to finding common ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:30:19-07:00","id":896186,"title":"","content":"Indeed I'm looking for an hunter archetipe able to interact with the supernatural beings even without a gun. I don't want neither an extremist or a gooder, but I'm looking for something balanced. So I came out with a bizzarre concept: a catholic priest which is also a former soldier! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:01:29-07:00","id":896240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/892009-building-my-reckoning-s-hunter?p=896186#post896186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed I'm looking for an hunter archetipe able to interact with the supernatural beings even without a gun. I don't want neither an extremist or a gooder, but I'm looking for something balanced. So I came out with a bizzarre concept: a catholic priest which is also a former soldier! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably not that bizarre. A retired chaplain, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:58:12-07:00","id":896290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/892009-building-my-reckoning-s-hunter?p=896240#post896240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's probably not that bizarre. A retired chaplain, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a soldier who got tired of war, so found peace in god...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T19:09:53-07:00","id":903187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/892009-building-my-reckoning-s-hunter?p=894561#post894561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but for me it was always strange how a group of super powered individuals dedicated to hunting DOWN all other supers, would have those supers as allies/friends/contacts...</div> </div> </div> </div>Says the Wayward <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T21:33:36